From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] libzfs: relay sockets to the kernel as pipes are

XNU lets the module do I/O only on a vnode, so libzfs_macos_wrapfd()
gives zfs send and zfs receive a FIFO and relays a pipe through it. A
socket needs the same, and ksh93 (the OpenZFS test suite's shell) makes
its pipelines of socketpairs: zfs send | zfs recv in a test passed the
kernel a socket, which panicked it in spl_vn_rdwr() and, since patch
0007, fails with "Bad file descriptor" (zfs_send-b,
zfs_receive_to_encrypted and others, P3-01 checkpoint 2). Sockets are
relayed now too.

Rebase-risk: low
---
diff --git a/lib/libzfs/os/neodarwin/libzfs_util_os.c b/lib/libzfs/os/neodarwin/libzfs_util_os.c
--- a/lib/libzfs/os/neodarwin/libzfs_util_os.c
+++ b/lib/libzfs/os/neodarwin/libzfs_util_os.c
@@ -503,8 +503,17 @@
 	if (error != 0)
 		return;
 
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+	/*
+	 * ksh93 makes its pipelines of socketpairs, which the kernel can't
+	 * do I/O on either: relay a socket as a pipe.
+	 */
+	if (!S_ISFIFO(sb.st_mode) && !S_ISSOCK(sb.st_mode))
+		return;
+#else
 	if (!S_ISFIFO(sb.st_mode))
 		return;
+#endif
 
 	if (pipe_relay_pid != 0) {
 #ifdef VERBOSE_WRAPFD
